1.Gauss’s Law
it describes how electric charges create electric fields.

Divergence measures how much a field behaves like a source (fountain) 
or a sink (drain) at a specific point in space.

Positive Divergence (> 0)    Negative Divergence (< 0)    Zero Divergence (= 0)
        (Fountain)                    (Drain)                   (Pass-Through)

The symbol $\nabla$ (called "nabla" or "del") represents spatial differentiation across 3D coordinates ($x, y, z$):

For an isolated positive point charge the force on a positive test charge is directed away from the centre, 
and so the field is also directed away from the centre.

On the other hand for an isolated negative point charge the force on the test charge is in the opposite direction, 
and so the field is directed towards the centre.
